    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tests the behavior when fog is enabled but the fog coordinate is not specified by the shader.</para>
<para>This test reproduces behavior observed in &quot;Blade 2&quot; <ulink url="https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu/issues/1852">https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu/issues/1852</ulink></para>
<para>Observations from HW:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>A draw that cannot write anything (color, depth, and stencil all disabled) still updates the carried fog values.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Carried fog is tracked per vertex rather than as a single value. For vertices submitted inline (immediate mode SET_VERTEX, inline buffers, and inline arrays) a vertex that does not write fog inherits the fog of the vertex six positions earlier in submission order. The association continues across draws and does not depend on whether the primitives are points or triangles. This is consistent with six vertex output buffers used round robin.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For vertices fetched from memory (draw arrays and inline elements) the inherited values have no stable pattern and differ between runs, presumably depending on the timing of vertex fetch relative to shader execution.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Waiting for the pushbuffer to become idle between draws changes the association; the six vertex pattern above does not predict the results of CarryoverNopDraw, which waits between its draws. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
